@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Neural Networks — Selection Map (depth, weight sharing, credit assignment)
' Synthesis of the pre-transformer neural family; the LLM tiers sit at L5-L7 of the ladder
' Level:  1

actor "Human expert\ninput structure?" as H

component "Perceptron\nsingle linear threshold" as P <<app>>
component "MLP\nhidden layers + non-linearity" as MLP <<app>>
component "CNN\nweight sharing over a grid" as CNN <<host>>
component "Backpropagation\nreverse-mode credit assignment" as BP <<async>>

H ARROW_OPTIONAL P : historical floor —\nlinearly separable only
H ARROW_MAIN MLP : unstructured feature vector
H ARROW_MAIN CNN : local structure and\ntranslation invariance
MLP ARROW_MAIN BP : how the weights are learned
CNN ARROW_MAIN BP

note bottom of BP
  **Backprop is the enabling idea, not a topology:**
  it makes credit assignment through hidden layers
  cheap, which is what let depth become useful
  (""backpropagation.puml"").
  It computes gradients; the update rule that
  consumes them is ""../optimization/"".
  ----
  **Ladder note.** These are the pre-LLM primers.
  Adapting a pretrained network's //weights// is
  Level 5 (""_spec/study-cases/5-fine-tuned/""); doing it against a
  reward loop is Level 6 (""_spec/study-cases/6-post-training/"").
end note
@enduml
